.TITLE "wc"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays word, line, and byte counts. It analyzes __text files__ and provides statistical information about their contents.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**wc file**
Displays the line, word, and byte counts for a file.
> __file__ the target path

**wc -l file**
Displays only the total number of lines in a file.
> __-l__ line count flag

**wc -w file**
Displays only the total number of words in a file.
> __-w__ word count flag

**wc -c file**
Displays only the total number of bytes in a file.
> __-c__ byte count flag

**wc -m file**
Displays the total number of characters in a file.
> __-m__ character count flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __wc -l__ command is frequently used in pipelines to count the number of results returned by other commands like __ls__ or __grep__. Always remember that the word count depends on the default whitespace delimiters.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ls** **mac:grep**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/wc.html__
